 "entryNodeId": "base",
 "rationale": "Two printed parts are needed because the platform slides relative to the base. The driven prismatic joint mints the NEMA 17, the 5x8 coupler, the T8 screw and the flanged nut. The guide joint mints the 8 mm rod and the LM8UU, and the joint rules cut every mount and seat. Bosses carry the rod socket and the 24 mm bearing, which do not fit in 8 mm plates.",
 "design": "Sturdy functional machine parts: flat plates with a 1 mm chamfer on outside edges and generous fillets where the bosses meet the plates. Walls should read solid rather than skeletal, with no decoration, so the base and platform look like one matched mechanism.",
